hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"641","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha in Muhsab, then slept a little. Then (later) they rode towards the House of Allah and circumambulated it. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"642","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that she did not stay at Abtah (Muhasab) and she used to say that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed at this place because it was easier to return from here. (Narrated by Muslim)."
"643","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered the people that their last act should be circumambulation of the House of Allah, but it has been reduced for menstruating women. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"644","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The reward of offering one prayer in this mosque of mine is a thousand times greater than offering prayers in other mosques, except the Masjid al-Haram.\" And performing one prayer in Masjid Haram is better than offering a hundred prayers in this mosque.” (Narrated by Ahmad and authenticated by Ibn Hibban.)"
"645","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was stopped (at Hudaybiyah), he shaved his head, married his wives and slaughtered sacrificial animals, then performed Umrah the following year. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"646","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Zubayah bint Zubair bin Abdul Muttalib. He said: O Messenger of Allah! I intend to perform Hajj but I am ill. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition that the place where I will open my Ihram will be where, O Allah! You stopped me.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"647","Hazrat Ikramah narrated from Hajjaj bin Amr Ansari that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"If a person breaks a bone or becomes lame, then he has become halal (out of Ihram). Now it is obligatory for him to perform Hajj next year.\" (It has been narrated by all five and Tirmidhi has described it as Hasan.)"
"648","It was narrated from Hazrat Rafa' bin Rafi' that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, \"Which earning is more pure?\" He said: \"The earnings of a man's own hand and every kind of trade that is free from deceit and deceit.\" (Narrated by Bazar and confirmed by Hakim)."
"649","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say in Makkah in the year of the conquest of Makkah: \"Indeed, Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the trade in wine, dead pigs, and idols.\" He was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about dead animal fat? Because with it boats are gilded and hides are lubricated and people burn it for light. He said: \"No, that too is forbidden.\" Then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"May Allah spoil the Jews.\" When Allah made fat forbidden to them, they melted it and sold it and ate its price.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"650","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, who says: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: \"When there is a dispute between the seller and the buyer, and no one has evidence or testimony, then the owner of the property will be valid, or both of them should abandon the transaction.\""
"651","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Mas'ud Ansari that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a wicked woman, and the sweets of a priest. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"652","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was traveling on one of his tired camels. He decided to leave her. It is narrated by Hazrat Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me from behind. You prayed for me and hit the camel and it started to run faster than it had ever run before. He said: \"Sell me this camel for one ounce of silver.\" I said: No! He then said again: \"Sell me this camel.\" So I sold it to you for one ounce of silver and stipulated that I would ride it to my family. So, as soon as I reached (Madinah), I took that camel and came to your service. You paid me the cash price for it.' Then I returned (after receiving the money) and you sent (a camel too) after me and said: 'Did you think about me that I lowered the price so that I could take your camel?' Take your camel and keep the money with you, so it is for you.” (Bukhari and Muslim) This context is in Muslim."
"653","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that one of us made his slave a slave. He had no wealth except this slave. The Prophet called this slave and sold him. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"654","It is narrated from Hazrat Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, that a mouse fell into ghee and died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it, and he said: \"Take it out and throw it out and throw out the ghee around it and use (the remaining ghee).\""
"655","Hazrat Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When a rat falls into ghee, if the ghee is frozen, throw out the rat and the ghee around it, and if the ghee is liquid, do not break even near it.\""
"656","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Zubayr (may Allah have mercy on him) that I asked Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) about the price of a bat and a dog. (Muslim and Feminine) and Feminine has this addition: \"Except for a hunting dog.\""
"657","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said that Hazrat Barirah (the maid) came to me and said: I have written to my owners for nine (9) ounces of silver that I will continue to pay one ounce every year, so help me (in this matter). I said: If your owners like me to pay your total amount in one lump sum and your villa will be for me, then I am ready to do so. Hazrat Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) went to her owners with this proposal and told them this, but they refused to accept it. Hazrat Berira (RA) came back to him. At that time, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was also present. Barira said: I made that proposal to my owners but they refused to accept it and they say that the villa will be for them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard this and Hazrat Aisha (RA) also informed the Prophet (PBUH) about this incident, so he said: \"Take him and make a condition of the villa with him, because the rightful owner of the villa is the one who gives freedom.\" Hazrat Aisha did the same. After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to address the people. Praise be to Allah, the Exalted.” Then he said: “What has happened to the people that they impose such conditions that are not in the Book of Allah. (Remember that) every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is void, even if there are hundreds of conditions. Allah's judgment is very true and Allah's condition is very firm and firm. And the villa belongs to the one who frees. (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are Bukhari's. ) and the words of Muslim are that he said: \"Buy him and set him free and make a condition of a villa with him.\" \"."
"658","There is a hadith on the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that Hazrat Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, forbade the sale of Umm-Wald and said: It cannot be sold, it cannot be gifted, nor can it be divided into inheritance. He can benefit from it as long as the owner wants and when the owner dies, he is free. (It has been narrated by Bayhaqi and Malik and they have said that some have called it Marfoo, which is an illusion.)"
"659","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who says that we used to sell the women and children of slave girls in the presence of the Prophet (peace be upon him). You didn't see any ugliness in it. (Nasa’i, Ibn Majah, and Darqutni narrated it all three, and Ibn Hibban called it Sahih.)"
"660","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of water in excess of what is needed. (Muslim) And there is this addition in a hadith: And you have also prohibited taking compensation for a pair of camels."
"661","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the payment of a male mate. (Bukhari)"
"662","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the marriage of Habal-Hablah. And this sale was in the period of Jahiliyyah (in this way) that a man would buy a camel on the condition that he would pay its price when the camel gave birth to a child, then the child in the camel's belly would give birth (to another child). (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are Bukhari's)"
"663","It is also narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of a villa and its donation. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"664","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade trade by throwing pebbles and trade by deception. (Muslim)"
"665","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever buys grain, he should not sell it (further) until he measures it.\" (Muslim)"
"666","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two pledges in one pledge. (It has been narrated by Ahmada and Nasa'i, and Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban have declared it to be authentic.) And it is in the tradition of Abu Dawud: (The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said:) \"Whoever makes two deals in one deal, he will either get less or else he will take interest.\""
"667","Hazrat Amr ibn Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with him) who says that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Loan and sale (together) are not lawful, nor are two conditions lawful in one sale.\" And it is not permissible to profit from a thing before taking possession of it. And it is not permissible or halal to sell what you do not have. (This hadith has been narrated by Al-Tabarani in the same manner and it is poor.)"
"668","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of Arabs. (It was narrated by Imam Malik, may God have mercy on him. And he said: I have received this tradition from Amr bin Shuaib.)"
"669","It is narrated from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: I bought oil (olive) from the market. When my deal was settled, I found a man who offered me a good profit. I decided to make a deal with this man.' Meanwhile, someone grabbed my arm from behind. I turned around and saw that it was Hazrat Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: Do not sell it at the place where you bought it, even if you carry it to your house, because the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling things from where they are bought, unless the merchants and traders take the purchased goods to their homes. (It was narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud, and these words are Abu Dawud's, and Ibn Hibban and Hakim called it Sahih.)"
"670","On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he says: I said: O Messenger of Allah! I trade camels in Baqi. I sell in dinars and receive dirhams and (sometimes) I sell in dirhams and receive dinars (ie) I take dinars in exchange for dirhams and give dirhams in exchange for dinars. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \"There is no problem if you exchange them with your brother on the same day, and before you both separate from each other, no part of the money remains due to anyone.\""
"671","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade impurity. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"672","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the pledge of allegiance, Muzabnah, Mukhabara and Sanya, but in this case (Bay Sanya) is permissible if it is determined. (It has been narrated by all five except Ibn Majah and Tirmidhi has declared it Sahih.)"
"673","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Anas, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade buying, selling, makhadira, mulamsa, manabza and muzabna. (Bukhari)"
"674","Hazrat Tawas narrates on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. He says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not go ahead and meet the merchant caravans, and let no citizen sell the goods of a villager.\" He said: Citizens should not become pimps of villagers. (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are Bukhari's)"
"675","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not go ahead and meet those who bring grain to the city from outside.\" (The merchant) who was met on the way and bought his goods, after reaching the market, the owner of the goods (the merchant) has the right (whether to keep the deal or to cancel it) (Muslim)."
"676","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a citizen to sell the goods of a villager. And (said): \"If you do not intend to buy a deal, do not raise the price.\" And no one should marry his brother's marriage, nor should he marry his brother's marriage. And no woman should demand the divorce of her (Muslim) sister in order to get what is her share."
"677","There is a hadith on the authority of Abu Ayyub Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: \"Whoever separates a mother from her child, Allah will separate her and her loved ones on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"678","On the authority of Hazrat Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to sell two slave brothers. I sold them both to separate men and then I mentioned it to you, so you said: \"Go and bring them back and sell them both together.\""
"679","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that he says that during the reign of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, the prices of things rose in Madinah. People said: O Messenger of Allah! The prices of commodities have become (big) fast, you fix (their) prices for us. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah is the One who determines the price, He is the one who restricts, the one who gives generously, and the one who provides.\" I want that when I meet Allah Ta'ala, no one will ask me for life and wealth on the grounds of oppression."
"680","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Muammar bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrates from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “No one hoards except a sinner.” (Muslim)"
"681","Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: \"(When selling) do not stop the milk of camels and sheep in their udders. If a person buys such an animal, after milking it, he has the right to choose the better of two things, whether he keeps the animal and if he wants to return it with a saa of dates.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in the tradition of Muslim, it is: \"He has the right for three days.\" Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, states that dates are mentioned in most hadiths."
"682","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that whoever buys a goat whose milk has stopped in its udders, and then returns it, then he should return one Sa'a with it. (Bukhari) and Ismaili have narrated the addition that one saa is dates."
"683","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a pile of grain. As you inserted your hand into it, your fingers felt moist. He said: \"O owner of grains! What is this?'' He said: O Messenger of Allah! It had rained on him. He said: \"Then why did you not put it (moistened part) on top of the grain so that the (buyers) could see it?\" Whoever cheated has nothing to do with me.” (Muslim)"
"684","Hazrat Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father Hazrat Burida (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever withholds the grapes during their harvest to sell them to a winemaker will enter Hellfire knowingly.”"
"685","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The one who is entitled to the income is the one who is the guarantor.\""
"686","It is narrated from Hazrat Urwa Baraqi (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) gave him one dinar to buy a sacrificial animal or a goat. He bought two goats for one dinar, then sold one of them for one dinar and came to your service with one goat and one dinar. You prayed for them to be blessed in their trade, so they were like that even if they bought soil, they would definitely get profit from it too. (All five of them have narrated it, except Nasa'i, and Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, narrated it in the context of a hadith, but he did not quote these words, and Tirmidhi narrated the hadith narrated by Hazrat Hakim bin Hizam, may God be pleased with him, as a witness for him.)"
"687","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying the babies of animals before they were born, and forbade buying the milk (collected) in their udders, and forbade the buying of a runaway slave, and forbade the buying of booty before it was distributed, and forbade the buying of alms before it was seized, and forbade the purchase of a diver’s dive (in advance). (It was narrated by Ibn Majah, Bazar and Darqutni with a weak chain of transmission.)"
"688","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not buy the fish in the water, for it is deceitful.\""
"689","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the sale of fruits before they are (ripe and) edible, and also forbade the sale of wool on the backs of animals and milk in the udders. (This hadith was narrated by Tabarani in his middle and by Darqutani. And Abu Dawud narrated it in Ikrima’s Murasil and this is Rajih. Also, it was narrated by Abu Dawud with a strong chain of transmission from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, and Bayhaqi preferred it.)"
"690","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the buying and selling of articles and medicines. (It was narrated by Bazar and its chain of transmission is weak.)"
"691","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever returns the goods sold from a Muslim, Allah will forgive his sins and misdeeds.”"
"692","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) that he said: \"When two men begin to bargain with each other, each of them has authority until they stay together and do not separate from each other\" or they give authority to each other. If one \"gives authority to the other\" and then the deal is settled on it, then the deal is complete. And if they separate from each other after making the deal, and neither of them has canceled the pledge, then the pledge will be valid.” (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are from Muslim)"
"693","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father (Shuaib) from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"The buyer and the seller have authority until they separate\" unless the transaction is an authority. And it is not permissible to leave hastily because of the fear of returning the bargain.”"
"694","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that a person was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) that he was usually cheated in marriage. He (called him) and said: \"When making a deal, say that there will be no deception.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"695","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (SAW) cursed the usury taker, the giver, the person who wrote it and its witnesses, and said: “All of them are equal and equal (in the commission of sin).”"
"696","Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “There are seventy-three levels of usury. The lowest degree is like the sin of a man marrying his own mother. And above all usury is to disgrace a Muslim."
"697","Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not sell gold for gold, but equal.\" Do not add to each other's weight. And do not sell silver for silver, but equal, and do not add to each other's weight. And do not sell the loan in exchange for cash.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"698","On the authority of Hazrat Ubada bin Samit, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt, equally and in cash. If there is a difference in the goods, then sell as you wish, provided that (the exchange of goods on both sides) is in cash.\" (Muslim)"
"699","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Exchange gold for gold (when it is equal in weight and likeness) and silver for silver (when it is equal in weight and likeness.\" Then if a person gives more or demands more, it is interest.\" (Muslim)"
"700","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri and Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a person to be in charge of Khaibar. So he came to his service with very good dates. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: \"Are all the dates that grow in Khaybar like this?\" He said: No, O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! We give other dates two sa's and (sometimes) three sa's, and these dates take one sa'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Do not do this. Sell bad dates for a dirham, then buy good dates with a dirham.'' And he said the same about weighing items. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in Muslim it is: \"Do the same in Tul.\""
"701","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of a pile of dates that has not been measured in exchange for a fixed measure of dates. (Muslim)"
"702","It was narrated from Hazrat Muammar bin Abdullah (RA) that I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"Food (grain) should be equal (in quantity) to food.\" In those days, our food was barley. (Muslim)"
"703","It was narrated from Hazrat Fazla bin Ubaid (RA) that I bought a necklace for twelve dinars on the day of Khaibar. It had jewels of gold and stone. I took them apart and found more than twelve dinars of gold in them. I mentioned it to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: \"It should not be sold until they are separated.\" (Muslim)"
"704","It is narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade selling an animal on loan for an animal. (All five have narrated it, and Tirmidhi and Ibn Jarood have declared it authentic.)"
"705","On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “When you start trading in mirrors, grab the tails of oxen, love agriculture and farming, and abandon Jihad, then Allah will bring humiliation upon you.” He will not remove this (humiliation) from you until you return to your religion.”"
"706","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever makes an intercession for his brother (after that), he gives him a gift and he accepts it, then he has reached the door of usury.”"
